enforced at runtime | No runtime validation despite type hints |\n\n## Root 
Cause\nPython dataclasses don't enforce type hints at runtime. The 
`WorkingMemoryEntry` constructor accepts any type for `lines_read`, which 
violates the `str` type hint. While `_parse_line_ranges` handles `None` and 
non-string values gracefully (returns empty list), this is a type safety issue 
that could lead to subtle bugs.\n\n## Fix Plan\nAdd `__post_init__` validation 
to `WorkingMemoryEntry` to ensure `lines_read` is either a string or `None` (for
deserialization).\n\n## Status: FIXED\n\n## Files Changed\n1. 
